 "about_text": "√K Contemporary is a contemporary art gallery in the Kagurazaka district of Tokyo, opened in March 2020 by SEI-RIN Co., Ltd., the company behind the long-established Japanese art dealer Kashima Arts. Its 300-square-metre space was designed around an 'outer space' concept, intended to present works with new values and perspectives. The gallery focuses on introducing a new generation of Japanese and international artists working across painting, photography, sculpture and new media, while situating their work within the broader lineage of Japanese art history. Below the main gallery, Space √K offers an industrial concrete basement rentable for exhibitions, fashion shows, and performances. The gallery regularly participates in major regional art fairs and has been featured in international art press.",
